In article <1992Jul24.163610.16464@wdl.loral.com> dcb@wdl1.wdl.loral.com (David C Blume) writes:
>How about a new character, the "Handsome Man/Woman?"
>
>This character would start off with a mirror, and a lot of gold.  The
>beginning stats for the Handsome Man would have very high Charisma (18/03),
>and very low everything else.
>
>The Handsome Man gets very good prices at shops.
>
>When encountering critters, all critters of the same alignment (Lawful) 
>have to save versus taming, in which case they become pets.  Neutral
>critters are intimidated about attacking such a Handsome man, so they
>almost never do.  Furthermore, the Handsome Man gets "Safe Pet" warnings
>preventing him from attacking Lawfuls and Neutrals.  (A Handsome Man
>would never do anything like *that!*)  Chaotics may occasionally attack
>the Handsome Man out of jealousy, but all he has to do is apply the mirror
>at the critter, and the critter will be so shamed for being so hideous in
>comparison with the Handsome Man that it will instantly flee.  The Handsome
>Man may attack a Chaotic (After answering 'y' to the "Do something 
>unhandsome?" prompt.)  The attacked critter will be so shaken by being
>attacked by such a Handsome Man, that the critter will almost always flee.
>
>The wizard will be shocked to see such a Handsome Man in hell.  The wizard
>is also very happy, because all he ever sees down is hell are hardened
>adventurers.  The wizard will pummel the Handsome Man in one round and 
>kill him instantly.  (The Handsome Man has a *very* hard time getting 
>experience points.)  Examining the corpse, the wizard will feel very very
>bad about killing such a Handsome Man.
>
